      <h2>Security & Role Isolation Suite</h2>
      <p>
        All 18 automated security attack tests pass with zero vulnerabilities.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Judge Isolation:</strong> An assigned judge attempting to query peer evaluations receives an explicit <code>403 Forbidden</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Participant Protection:</strong> Hackathon participants cannot access raw or unreleased judge scores.</li>
        <li><strong>Data Export Shielding:</strong> An unauthenticated visitor or participant attempting to trigger <code>/api/export.csv</code> receives <code>401 Unauthorized</code> or <code>403 Forbidden</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Cross-Event Shielding:</strong> Organizers are isolated to their own events; cross-event workspace access is denied.</li>
        <li><strong>Rubric Integrity:</strong> Submitting invented criteria or unassigned project scores is strictly rejected.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cloud Infrastructure & Deployment</h2>
      <p>
        Judgely is engineered for both 100% offline self-hosting and Firebase Cloud operation:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Self-Hosted Mode (Default):</strong> Pure SQLite, zero cloud dependencies, offline-first. Runs natively with Docker.</li>
        <li><strong>Firebase Hosting:</strong> Target <code>judgely</code> at <code>https://judgely.web.app</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Firebase Firestore:</strong> Default database with compiled security rules (<code>firestore.rules</code>) enforcing zero-trust client access.</li>
        <li><strong>Firebase Authentication:</strong> Identity Toolkit configuration supporting Google Identity Services and session exchange.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Interactive Health Check</h2>
      <p>Test the active backend response directly from your browser:</p>
      <div style="background:var(--bg-card);border:1px solid var(--border-line);padding:16px;border-radius:4px;margin-top:12px;">
